# What the SOURCE distribution carries: the wrapper, its tests, its examples
# and its Makefile. No native library -- an sdist is pure Python, and a
# library inside one would be a library for the wrong machine.
#
# The wheel is the other half of the pair: a wheel job copies `libsekejap`
# into `python/sekejap/_lib/` first, and `[tool.setuptools.package-data]`
# puts it in the wheel. Build the sdist from a tree with no staged library
# (`make sdist` removes one), because a MANIFEST rule that pruned it here
# would take it out of the wheel as well.
include README.md
include Makefile
include bench.py
graft examples
graft tests
global-exclude __pycache__ *.py[cod]
